From: Le Hoang Quyen <lehoangquyen@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:40:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/22] [M156] gpu: Use kVaapi stream for
 CompoundImageBacking::ProduceVideo

Original change's description:
> gpu: Use kVaapi stream for CompoundImageBacking::ProduceVideo
>
> Previously, CompoundImageBacking::ProduceVideo used kGL backing which
> created GLTextureImageBacking. However, GLTextureImageBacking doesn't
> really support video. Its ProduceVideo (via
> D3D11VideoImageCopyRepresentation::CreateFromGL) is incorrect because
> it copies the GL texture into a separate D3D11 texture eagerly during
> ProduceVideo() and does not synchronize with the BeginAccess/EndAccess
> path. Any content synced by CompoundImageBacking::NotifyBeginAccess
> or written to the SharedImage after ProduceVideo() is missed.
>
> Remove GLTextureImageBacking::ProduceVideo and CreateFromGL, disallow
> SharedImageAccessStream::kVaapi in GLTextureImageBacking and
> WrappedGraphiteTextureBacking, and update
> CompoundImageBacking::ProduceVideo to request kVaapi (with both
> VIDEO_DECODE and VIDEO_ENCODE_ACCELERATOR usages) instead of kGL so a
> video-capable backing (such as D3DImageBacking on Windows) is
> allocated and synchronized on BeginAccess/EndAccess.
>
